  "definitions": {
    "priceToIncome": "OECD nominal house price index for Australia divided by ABS household gross disposable income per capita, seasonally adjusted, indexed to 1996 = 100. Income is divided by estimated resident population. This is a relative price measure. It is not a household affordability measure.",
    "priceToRent": "OECD house price to rent ratio, indexed to 1996 = 100. The ratio is the inverse of the gross rental yield. A net cap rate after vacancy, operating costs and depreciation would be lower, but the expense ratio is stable over long periods, so the ranking is similar. The series begins in 1972; the figure starts in 1981, and the earlier observations are below 100.",
    "ladder": "Each row holds disposable income and rents at their current levels and moves only the price of the dwelling stock. Price-to-income and price-to-rent are indices, 1996 = 100. The 0% row uses 2026-Q1 for price-to-income and 2025-Q3 for price-to-rent."
  },
